course: dictionary
lesson: 4247
title: One word, many meanings: grape
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can be a plain fruit in one sentence and a warning in another. The dictionary says a grape is a small, round, juicy fruit that grows in bunches on a vine. To find out which meaning the writer wants, read the words around grape.
explain: «Chocolate, grapes and the sweetener xylitol can poison dogs.» Here grapes is a danger, because the words around it talk about poison. Grapes can also be a healthy snack, but this sentence is a warning about pets.
explain: Some words look like English but mean something else in another language. «Le raisin» is French, and it means grapes. In English, a raisin is a dried grape, so the same fruit gets a new name once it has been dried.
fact: A grape is a small, round, juicy fruit that grows in bunches on a vine.
fact: Grapes can be green, red or purple.
fact: Grapes are poisonous to dogs, so never give them to pets.
fact: Whole grapes can get stuck in a small child's throat, so cut them lengthways into quarters for toddlers.
fact: Dried grapes are raisins, sultanas and currants.
exercise: «Chocolate, grapes and the sweetener xylitol can poison dogs.» What is the danger in this sentence? | Grapes are too sweet for breakfast | *Grapes can poison dogs | Grapes must be washed before eating | Grapes make dogs grow larger
exercise: In English, what is a raisin? | *A dried grape | A green grape on a vine | A kind of bread | A small bird
exercise: Why cut grapes into quarters for a toddler? | Quarters taste sweeter | *Whole grapes can get stuck in a small child's throat | Quarters stop the grapes going brown | Quarters make the grapes easier to count
test: A grape is a small, round fruit that grows on what? | A tree trunk | A cloud | A rock | *A vine
test: Grapes are made into which two drinks? | *Juice and wine | Milk and tea | Cola and lemonade | Soup and water
exam: In «Chocolate, grapes and the sweetener xylitol can poison dogs», how do you know grapes is a warning and not a snack? | *The words around it say grapes can poison dogs | The sentence is about breakfast | It is written in capital letters | Grapes are always dangerous to people
